From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bryson <10244083+brysonwf@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 09:55:38 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: qcom_smbx: return an error from
 smb_get_prop_health() for unknown generations

The switch over chip->gen has no default case, so the function could fall off its end without a return value
(-Wreturn-type). Return -EINVAL.

This patch was written by Claude (Anthropic's AI assistant) under the direction of Bryson, who reviewed and
tested it on a Surface Duo.

Signed-off-by: Bryson <10244083+brysonwf@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbx.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbx.c b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbx.c
index b723dba5b..1e2776f14 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbx.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbx.c
@@ -585,6 +585,7 @@ static int smb_get_prop_health(struct smb_chip *chip, int *val)
 	case SMB5:
 		return smb5_get_prop_health(chip, val);
 	}
+	return -EINVAL;
 }
 
 static int smb_get_property(struct power_supply *psy,
